module effect_e_name.neg_1

// `Effect[T]` (D87/D142, the builtin generic type of a handler's value) is
// a known type WORD now (2026-09-21), not a typo -- and it still refuses,
// but honestly.
//
// WHY THIS FIXTURE. Before the fix, `Effect[T]` in a parameter or return
// position gave "undeclared type name `Effect`" -- and the name is not
// undeclared, it is a genuine language word this subset's registry does
// not hold, exactly the class `is_language_type_word` already carries
// `unit`/`never`/`any` for. This fixture pins the DIFFERENT, honest
// refusal the flow reaches once the name stops lying: the existing
// subset-debt message about an unknown type shape, unchanged by this fix
// and already dated. A regression of `check/typeref_rules.nv`'s
// `is_language_type_word` list would silently fall back to the wrong
// "undeclared" text.

// NOVAC_EXPECT novac does not know this type yet

fn pass_through(x Effect[int]) -> Effect[int] => x

fn main() {
    println(1)
}
